1. The text argues that God creates everything, including all possibilities, and that we are subjective vessels (qualia) whose experiences are shaped by choice. Suffering and evil are not objective cosmic facts but are chosen or believed into existence through our subjective perspective. Therefore, we retain agency to change our experience, even if we feel trapped.

