1. The text argues that God creates everything, including all possibilities, and that we are subjective vessels—qualia—whose experiences are shaped by choice. Suffering and evil are not objective cosmic facts but are chosen or believed into existence through our subjective perspective. Therefore, we retain agency to change our experience, even if we feel trapped.

2. I partly agree: perception, attention, and belief can amplify or reduce suffering, and agency matters. But I disagree that all suffering is simply chosen; much is caused by illness, violence, injustice, and circumstances beyond individual control. The text risks blaming victims and ignoring real constraints.

3.  
If God creates all things,  
The joy and pain life brings,  
Our qualia paints the view,  
We choose what we pursue.  
Though suffering feels real and deep,  
We still can move, and choose, and leap. [end of text]


